vhost: inherit the context's log context when info->log_cx is NULL

lws_create_vhost() bound a vhost created without info->log_cx to the
process-global log_cx, even when its context was created with its own
log_cx.  The internal "system" vhost (created from a zeroed info in
lws_create_context(), e.g. for async DNS) always took that path, and the
async-DNS UDP wsis inherit their log context from it.

With LWS_MAX_SMP == 1, lwsl_refcount_cx() updates the refcount without a
lock, so an application running one lws context per thread, each with its
own log_cx, still raced on the global log_cx's refcount through those
vhosts and wsis.  A lost update makes it reach 0 early and the next
decrement fails assert(cx->refcount) (txiki.js: Worker runtimes tearing
down concurrently in tests/test-tls-worker-concurrent.js).

Fall back to context->log_cx instead.  It is &log_cx unless the context was
given its own, so single-context users see no change.

Rebased onto v5.1.0 (5f39aa483): the code moved from lib/core-net/vhost.c
to lib/io/vhost.c (sans-io split, 4c1c0d6f2); the change is unchanged and
still not upstream (v5.1.0 and main d954e68f2 still bind &log_cx).

Upstreamable as is.

---
diff --git a/lib/io/vhost.c b/lib/io/vhost.c
index c7489bb5c..66a5d4805 100644
--- a/lib/io/vhost.c
+++ b/lib/io/vhost.c
@@ -166,7 +166,7 @@ lws_create_vhost(struct lws_context *context,
 	if (info->log_cx)
 		vh->lc.log_cx = info->log_cx;
 	else
-		vh->lc.log_cx = &log_cx;
+		vh->lc.log_cx = context->log_cx;
 
 #if defined(LWS_WITH_EVENT_LIBS)
 	vh->evlib_vh = (void *)&vh[1];
